# Explicit, not just left as a transitive pin -- sqlalchemy's own package
# metadata declares this as a hard install_requires, gated by a
# platform_machine marker that checks for "aarch64" (Linux's name for
# arm64). macOS reports "arm64" instead, so pip-compile run on this Mac
# evaluates the marker false and silently drops greenlet from the lock
# file -- even though every actual deploy target (linux/amd64 in CI/EC2,
# and the linux/arm64 image this Mac's Docker builds locally) evaluates it
# true, so pip demands it be present and hashed. This project never uses
# SQLAlchemy's async engine, so greenlet is otherwise dead weight -- but
# `pip install --require-hashes` still fails without it, since the
# dependency is declared unconditionally on those platforms regardless of
# whether the code ever imports it. See docs/decisions.md.
greenlet==3.5.4
